====================================================================================================
PART 0 -- is the recipe capable of moving a charge at all? Three independent measurements.
====================================================================================================
Mechanism, read from source: LOSE_CHARGE/GAIN_CHARGE set atom.charge and nothing else
(molecule.py:538-548); apply_recipe then calls update_charge() on every product
(family.py:1547); update_charge re-derives charge = valence - bonds - radicals - 2*lp
(molecule.py:596-598). Nothing on the right-hand side was touched, so the charge returns
to its starting value. Below: whether that is what actually happens.

(0a) apply the recipe by hand to three representative reactant pairs

  Li+ + H-   (entry 24)          in  [Li+] (+1) + [H-] (-1)
                                 out [Li+] (+1) + [H-] (-1)   IDENTICAL -- no charge moved
  O+ + O     (entry 13 partner)  in  [O+] (+1) + [O] (+0)
                                 out [O+] (+1) + [O] (+0)   IDENTICAL -- no charge moved
  Ar+ + N2   (entry 19)          in  [Ar+] (+1) + N#N (+0)
                                 out [Ar+] (+1) + N#N (+0)   IDENTICAL -- no charge moved

  3 of 3 demonstration pairs came back unchanged.

(0b) ask the family to generate reactions for those same reactants
     _create_reaction rejects a reaction whose products are its reactants
     (family.py:1757-1759), so an inert recipe shows up here as zero.

  Li+ + H-   (entry 24)          generate_reactions -> 0 reaction(s)
  O+ + O     (entry 13 partner)  generate_reactions -> 0 reaction(s)
  Ar+ + N2   (entry 19)          generate_reactions -> 0 reaction(s)

(0c) census of every recipe under input/kinetics/families/ that uses a charge action.
